      "id": "6ad0a020e4d21b81a794c2fe",
      "fieldData": {
       "acrm---key-feature-4-content": "<h3>Credit limits checked at the order</h3><p>Before a new order ships, the app checks the age of the customer's oldest open invoice. An order that breaks your rule waits for an approver, who releases it or keeps the hold.</p>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6aba7ac40efe4e6ac8693159",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---key-feature-1-content": "<h3>Purchase requests routed by dollar amount</h3><p>Anything under $500 goes to the requester's manager, requests up to $5,000 go to the department head, and larger ones add the CFO. Nina Park's $4,800 order for 12 design licenses skips the manager and lands in #approvals for Priya Shah. Once she approves, the bill is created in Xero.</p>",
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Approval Workflow Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"An approval workflow is the path a request takes until someone with authority approves or rejects it. It sets who reviews the request and in what order, what happens after each decision, and where the record of every step is kept.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an automated approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"Write one sentence that names the trigger and each approver's dollar limit, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a> turns it into a working app. Run a real request through it, then change any rule by prompting until the routing matches your policy.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is approval workflow software used for?\", \"a\": \"Approval workflow software is used to take a request in, send it to the people who must sign off, chase them when they stall, and store the outcome. The same engine serves unrelated kinds of request: a marketing team runs drafts through a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/content-approval-workflow'>content approval workflow</a>, while finance routes spend by amount.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a multi-level approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"A multi-level approval workflow sends a request through tiers set by amount or risk. A small purchase stops at the manager, a larger one adds the department head, and the largest add the CFO. Emergent builds the tiers from one sentence in the prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is approval workflow automation?\", \"a\": \"Approval workflow automation replaces email chains and spreadsheets with software that picks the approver, sends the reminder, and writes down the decision without anyone forwarding a message. Requests stop waiting in inboxes, and the record keeps itself.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a workflow and an approval process?\", \"a\": \"A workflow is any repeatable run of steps, like onboarding a supplier or publishing a post. An approval process is the stage inside it where someone with authority says yes or no, and that answer is recorded. The purchase request gets approved; the wider workflow then places the order and pays the bill.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up escalation in an approval workflow system?\", \"a\": \"Set up escalation in an approval workflow system as a clock on each step, and log every hop. When a reminder goes unanswered, the request moves up a level or to a named backup, and the requester can see who holds it now. Give every chain a final owner, such as the finance lead, so no request can stall past the last step.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there an approval workflow template to start from?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Each of the four use cases above comes with a prompt for purchase requests, invoices, contracts, or expenses. Change the amounts and the approver names, and the prompt becomes your template: a new policy is a new sentence, not a redesigned form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I build an audit trail into an approval workflow app?\", \"a\": \"Build the audit trail into the approval workflow app as one row per event: every submission, reminder, escalation, and decision, with the person and the time. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/document-approval-workflow'>document approval workflow</a> also ties each sign-off to the exact version approved. Emergent keeps these rows in a database you own, so auditors read the same records your dashboard shows.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields should approval process software use to route requests?\", \"a\": \"Approval process software should route on the fields that decide who signs: amount, department, and category. A rule might send IT purchases to the IT lead and marketing spend to the marketing director. Once a spend request clears its approvers, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/purchase-order'>purchase order automation</a> can turn it into the PO sent to the vendor.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
