      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Freight Broker Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is freight broker automation?\", \"a\": \"Freight broker automation is software that runs the repeat steps of brokering a load without a person keying each one: reading quote requests, checking carrier paperwork, collecting check-ins, and matching carrier invoices. People still decide the exceptions, such as a thin margin or a charge nobody agreed to.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up freight broker automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with a month of closed loads and a written list of hold rules, each with a number and an owner. Describe both in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>, which builds the app and its database. Then connect your TMS and replay past loads before the live inboxes go on.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which tasks can AI automation for freight brokers take over?\", \"a\": \"The tasks that arrive as text or documents: shipper quote emails, insurance certificates, proof of delivery, and carrier invoices. AI reads each one into fields, and anything it reads with low confidence goes to a rep to confirm. Pricing calls and carrier choice stay with your people.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can logistics automation send shippers a weekly capacity email?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The app can read next week's lanes where you have carriers lined up and email each shipper only the lanes they ship on, every Monday morning. For a list-based email with sign-ups and unsubscribes, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/newsletter'>newsletter automation</a> is the closer fit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I add carrier onboarding to freight broker automation?\", \"a\": \"Send each new carrier one upload link for the whole packet, and have the app check each file as it lands. The app collects W-9s and keeps payment records ready for 1099 reporting, though it does not file taxes. Add a reminder to the carrier rep 30 days before any certificate expires.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should freight broker automation match carrier invoices to the rate confirmation?\", \"a\": \"Yes, because the rate confirmation is the agreed price for that load. FreightWaves calls it a binding contract between the carrier and the broker. A charge missing from it is a question for billing before anyone pays it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can freight broker automation post loads that still need a carrier?\", \"a\": \"Yes, to any channel with an API. The app can post each load still uncovered 2 hours after booking to your carrier email list, with the lane and pickup window. Posting the same loads to LinkedIn or X is a job for <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/social-media'>social media automation</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does freight broker automation handle detention claims?\", \"a\": \"It checks each claim against the driver's check-ins, using the free time and hourly rate from the rate confirmation. Detention is charged when a truck is held beyond the agreed-upon free time for loading or unloading. The app counts the hours between the arrival and departure check-ins. A claim longer than the check-ins show waits for billing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What records should freight broker automation keep for every load?\", \"a\": \"Keep the quote, the rate confirmation, every check-in, the signed proof of delivery, and both invoices on one load record, along with who approved each hold. Emergent builds the app on a database you own, and a dispute months later starts from that single record.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does freight broker automation follow up on unanswered quotes?\", \"a\": \"With a rule on open quotes. If a shipper has not replied 24 hours after the quote went out, the app emails a short reminder with the rate and pickup date. After a second silence, it marks the quote lost for the rep to review. It is the same pattern <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/abandoned-cart'>abandoned cart automation</a> uses for online stores. With no task cap in Emergent, every open quote gets its follow-up.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
