      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Prior Authorization Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is prior authorization automation?\", \"a\": \"Prior authorization automation is software that checks each request against the payer's document list, tracks the decision, and flags what needs a person. HealthCare.gov defines the authorization as a decision by your health insurer or plan that a health care service, treatment plan, prescription drug, or durable medical equipment is medically necessary.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up prior authorization automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with one payer and one service your practice requests often. Describe its document checklist, the follow-up rule, and who works a late request in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>, which turns that prompt into a working app. Then link your scheduling system and run the tracker on past requests before a live one.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should prior authorization automation wait for a payer decision?\", \"a\": \"Set the wait to the payer's own decision window. Under a CMS final rule, impacted payers (excluding QHP issuers on the FFEs) must send decisions within 72 hours for expedited requests and seven calendar days for standard requests, and Medicare Advantage organizations are among them. For other payers, use the window each one publishes.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does prior authorization automation keep a request from going out incomplete?\", \"a\": \"It compares each request's attachments with a checklist you keep for that payer and service, and holds the request until they match. The coordinator sees which document is missing and attaches it before the request can be sent. Update the checklist the day a payer changes its policy.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can prior authorization automation read a payer's decision letter?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent builds the tracker so it reads a scanned or faxed decision letter into structured fields with AI, and a field read at low confidence goes to a person before the record is saved. Check the first 10 letters from each new payer by hand before you rely on the reading.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a prior authorization automation alert say?\", \"a\": \"Only that a request needs action, with its request number and a link that opens it in the app. Leave the patient's name, the service, and any diagnosis out of the message. Staff read those details after they sign in, where the app controls who can see each screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does prior authorization automation track approvals that are about to run out?\", \"a\": \"It stores the approved visits and the approval window on each request, then counts visits as they are used. Pick a trigger, such as 2 visits left or 14 days to go, that leaves time to send a renewal request. Emergent sets no task cap, however many approvals the practice tracks.\"}, {\"q\": \"How should prior authorization automation handle a denied request?\", \"a\": \"Log the denial with its reason and date, then open a task for the coordinator with a due date you choose. Beginning in 2026, impacted payers must provide a specific reason for denied prior authorization decisions under a CMS final rule. Whether to appeal or resubmit stays a decision for your clinicians and billing staff.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can prior authorization automation send requests straight to the payer?\", \"a\": \"Yes, where the payer offers an API for it. A CMS final rule requires impacted payers to implement and maintain a Prior Authorization API, which must be implemented beginning January 1, 2027. For a payer without one, the app prepares the complete request and a coordinator submits it through the payer's portal or by fax.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I measure whether prior authorization automation is working?\", \"a\": \"Compare two numbers each month against the month before you switched it on: requests sent back for missing documents, and approvals that expired before anyone renewed them. Emergent builds the tracker with a live dashboard that shows both. Review them by payer, since one slow payer can hide behind a good average.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
